# JavaScript Basics

## What is JavaScript?

JavaScript (JS) is a high-level, interpreted programming language used to make web pages interactive and dynamic.

It allows you to:
- Respond to user actions
- Update webpage content
- Validate forms
- Create animations
- Fetch data from servers
- Build complete web applications

JavaScript is one of the three core technologies of web development:

- HTML → Structure
- CSS → Styling
- JavaScript → Functionality

---

# Ways to Add JavaScript

## 1. Inline JavaScript

```html
<button onclick="alert('Hello!')">Click Me</button>
```

**Explanation:**
- JavaScript is written directly inside an HTML element.
- Suitable only for very small tasks.
- Not recommended for large projects.

---

## 2. Internal JavaScript

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Internal JS</title>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Hello JavaScript</h1>

<script>
    console.log("Welcome to JavaScript");
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

**Explanation:**
- JavaScript is written inside the `<script>` tag.
- Usually placed before the closing `</body>` tag.

---

## 3. External JavaScript (Recommended)

### HTML

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>External JS</title>
</head>
<body>

<h1>JavaScript Basics</h1>

<script src="script.js"></script>

</body>
</html>
```

### script.js

```javascript
console.log("Hello from External JavaScript");
```

**Explanation:**
- JavaScript code is stored in a separate `.js` file.
- Makes code reusable and easier to maintain.

